tests[1]:
  - command: npm run coverage
    path: test/lineage.test.ts
    scope: project
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: thresholds met
    note: promotion refuses past the approved budget and names the item to extend
close_reason: "Both assertions now discriminate, each verified by mutation.\n\nBudget exhaustion: the test promotes distinct candidates gen-c2 and gen-c3 against a two-permission approval, then registers gen-c4 and asserts the third promotion is refused, that the message reports 2 promotion(s) consumed rather than merely firing, and that it names the approval item to extend. Proof it exercises the counter: suppressing the increment inside countPromotedUnderApproval turns the suite red at 23 of 24. Before this case, that mutation passed.\n\nSorted traversal: both runs in the fixture now reach the evaluation environment, so only the sort decides which is reported, and the assertion names the lexicographically first id. Proof: removing the sort() turns the suite red at 23 of 24.\n\nrelease:check green, coverage still an exact 100/100/100 across 9 files."
body: ""
